{"title":"1995 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO\" title=\"1995 USAMO\"> 1995</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"USAMO\">USAMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9a5565b6f024d1cf330294f9d836d35e14cd89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, p \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> be an odd <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a>.  The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d49db41139b0b7302e0e217365d77793555e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)_{n \\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> is defined as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ced43b60d19edd513da432e1b3d6261265f2d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, a_0 = 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2e0eb78ed39610781b6f94fd806493a8a8ce60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 1, \\, \\ldots, \\, a_{p-2} = p-2 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" /> and, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e318daebd8a90dad0097b38f2c57d0126b12de35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n \\geq p-1, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bbd0cb155ee6dce5ee7069ea4e9059f654a23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, a_n \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> is the least positive integer that does not form an arithmetic sequence of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9a5565b6f024d1cf330294f9d836d35e14cd89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, p \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> with any of the preceding terms. Prove that, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d355fce2af566ceb80d3d58aa61382c5d0bb4c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bbd0cb155ee6dce5ee7069ea4e9059f654a23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, a_n \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> is the number obtained by writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fe67cd85ba57a3c30adc14b0b68a259e69d403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n \\,$\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d383b3d1ab3efe208ff6d0ce4212d5f7d2dbb0d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, p-1 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and reading the result in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16038f9fba8338c93d5275bc2aeaecb508a1deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A calculator is broken so that the only keys that still work are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df52614a703f138f2273f30bb4954527ea3443b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\sin, \\; \\cos,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9c561e76fb0d4f51d6e5e32c59ba4ec9c7e480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan, \\; \\sin^{-1}, \\; \\cos^{-1}, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd881c6b23858817681c2298c4c0f4c127e1e36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\tan^{-1} \\,$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> buttons.  The display initially shows 0. Given any positive rational number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52de567b2fb907d7c3c52c250babad1ad4be5a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> show that pressing some finite sequence of buttons will yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27d23e74c5dc135a9d69a0bc75edc98330ac011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />.   Assume that the calculator does real number calculations with infinite precision.  All functions are in terms of radians.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a nonisosceles, nonright triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f797b4e02926f855f2b23863d3ef23ee1378b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, ABC, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d6622e32855900deff0a0f879afb56b7abbf6eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, O \\,$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> denote the center of its circumscribed circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88ad89bf517c94da7ca31f716633d1cec0a9a79f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, A_1, \\, B_1, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614b42a53b43b2dd220b7182f53d27411e5439b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, C_1 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed5d2224b4db6ec592fd89ac89e71ea154df628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, BC, \\, CA, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff720ef32c3c47568bea85bb3f2df7ee9e38f24d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, AB, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.  Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8d766d7f22fc155f42eeaaf28451f7f5118b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, A_2 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is located on the ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fe63765419aa1cbd7e7e8d25f81677dc428aea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, OA_1 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138f86187b85d4f36165631a19dd73257c2e7d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\triangle OAA_1 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b453074f33c6cf2a5c5cfdb6f94bda407f821fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\triangle OA_2A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d9faa7c4bc18baed332d9b8c21b2a89a0af708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, B_2 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabf93996be450f2f161bae294c4ae60e48f56e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, C_2 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> on rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfafa2d49ed6804ea24524fbd188b8bf1bb74b43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, OB_1 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce97d3dab424ad3224129d085fed26d3923b7489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, OC_1, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, are defined similarly.  Prove that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/5728ed8172a294f84cba65810d42adf5e0994078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, AA_2, \\, BB_2, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce480a1d56a08827b236a8b6e681224642d3d807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, CC_2 \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" /> are concurrent, i.e. these three lines intersect at a point.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a268fc0efcf0a335c24b365335dd8f2f824e55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q_0, \\, q_1, \\,  q_2, \\ldots \\; \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"11\" /> is an infinite sequence of integers satisfying the following two conditions:<br />\n(i)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f56f267beb09dc6be17eef1ad72b3029a08874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, m-n \\,$\" width=\"51\" height=\"8\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d516234ebefd20c35a6ba919d601f55e465cab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q_m - q_n \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1ac45f66467001047c5c2d54eaa43b5b109da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, m &gt; n \\geq 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> <br />\n(ii) there is a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2cab31c9f3998a76a46b6b840b98ab1135de2873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, P \\,$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2daef6c3c9bfc293b34eca5bbbb0e06ff0fe7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, |q_n| &lt; P(n) \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/4570fcd64e6514153993aa53c694f576919c1ec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n$\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" />. <br />\nProve that there is a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e27e2d672dd10ad08898547b79d7afe029fc7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, Q \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb7274a3dfd514727685c227bf95e1188c6697a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q_n = Q(n) \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/4570fcd64e6514153993aa53c694f576919c1ec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n$\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that in a certain society, each pair of persons can be classified as either <i>amicable</i> or <i>hostile</i>. We shall say that each member of an amicable pair is a <i>friend</i> of the other, and each member of a hostile pair is a <i>foe</i> of the other.  Suppose that the society has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fe67cd85ba57a3c30adc14b0b68a259e69d403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, n \\,$\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" /> persons and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252bd9794edd4df96b45c8d9d775440a737db9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> amicable pairs, and that for every set of three persons, at least one pair is hostile.  Prove that there is at least one member of the society whose foes include <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123271d6b63afbce30018715324abf325d4671aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q(1 - 4q/n^2) \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" /> or fewer amicable pairs.  \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO\" title=\"1995 USAMO\">1995 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_USAMO\" title=\"1994 USAMO\">1994 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO\" title=\"1996 USAMO\">1996 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.unl.edu/amc/a-activities/a7-problems/USAMO-IMO/q-usamo/-tex/usamo1995.tex\">1995 USAMO Problems (TEX)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.unl.edu/amc/a-activities/a7-problems/USAMO-IMO/q-usamo/-pdf/usamo1995.pdf\">1995 USAMO Problems (PDF)</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043917\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 284/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8185/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.048      1 -total\n 59.36%    7.746      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 37.86%    4.940      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6379:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043917 and revision id 54723. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}